  {% when 'terms-and-conditions', 'terms' %}
    <h2>Terms and Conditions</h2>
    <p>Welcome to Books Bunny, an online bookstore bringing together books from a wide range of publishers for readers of all ages. By accessing our website, products, and services, you agree to comply with these terms and conditions.</p>
    <h3>1. General and Use of Services</h3>
    <p>These terms govern your use of our website and services. You agree to use the platform lawfully and respectfully. Unauthorised activities such as hacking, phishing, or distributing malicious content are prohibited.</p>
    <h3>2. Orders and Payments</h3>
    <p>All orders are subject to availability and confirmation of payment. Prices are displayed in INR and include applicable taxes unless stated otherwise. Books Bunny may cancel or reject orders due to errors, fraudulent activity, stock unavailability, or publisher fulfilment issues.</p>
    <h3>3. Shipping, Returns, and Refunds</h3>
    <p>We deliver within India and internationally, subject to logistics availability. Orders are typically dispatched within 3–4 business days. Returns are accepted for damaged or defective items within 7 days of delivery. Approved refunds are processed to the original payment method within 7–10 working days. Digital products such as eBooks and audiobooks are non-refundable.</p>
    <h3>4. Intellectual Property</h3>
    <p>Books sold on Books Bunny remain the intellectual property of their respective publishers and authors. Website content created by Books Bunny, including text, logos, images, and design, may not be copied or distributed without consent.</p>
    <h3>5. User Content, Privacy, and Liability</h3>
    <p>Users may post respectful reviews or comments that do not violate laws or third-party rights. Your use of the platform is also governed by our Privacy Policy. Books Bunny is not liable for indirect or consequential damages, and total liability is limited to the amount paid for the relevant product or service.</p>
    <h3>6. Governing Law</h3>
    <p>These terms are governed by the laws of India. Disputes will be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts in Delhi, India.</p>
