  {% when 'faq', 'faqs' %}
    <h2>Books Bunny – Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <h3>1. What is Books Bunny?</h3>
    <p>Books Bunny is an online bookstore that brings together books from a wide range of publishers, offering readers a single destination to discover and buy fiction, non-fiction, children's literature, poetry, educational books, and more.</p>
    <h3>2. What makes Books Bunny different?</h3>
    <p>Books Bunny is a multi-publisher marketplace, not tied to a single publishing house. This means a broader catalogue, more choice, and the convenience of ordering titles from different publishers in one order.</p>
    <h3>3. What kind of books do you sell?</h3>
    <p>We offer books across genres and publishers, including fiction, non-fiction, children's literature, poetry, educational books, and socially relevant titles for young adults and general readers.</p>
    <h3>4. Do you publish books yourselves?</h3>
    <p>No. Books Bunny is a bookstore, not a publisher. We sell books on behalf of the publishers and authors who hold the rights to them.</p>
    <h3>5. Do you accept bulk or institutional orders?</h3>
    <p>Yes. We accept bulk orders for schools, libraries, and organisations. Contact <a href="mailto:sales@unboundscript.com">sales@unboundscript.com</a> for special pricing and details.</p>
    <h3>6. Can publishers list their books on Books Bunny?</h3>
    <p>Yes. Publishers who would like their titles listed can reach out through our contact page to discuss onboarding.</p>
    <h3>7. What is your return policy?</h3>
    <p>We accept returns when a product is damaged, defective, or incorrect at delivery. Customers should raise a request within 3–5 days of receiving the order.</p>
    <h3>8. Do you offer refunds?</h3>
    <p>Approved refunds are issued to the original payment method once the returned product is verified.</p>
    <h3>9. Can I cancel my order?</h3>
    <p>Orders can be cancelled only before dispatch. Once dispatched, cancellation is not possible, though return eligibility may still apply.</p>
    <h3>10. What if I receive a damaged or incorrect book?</h3>
    <p>Contact support immediately with order details and clear images of the issue. We will review and arrange replacement or refund as appropriate.</p>
    <h3>11. Are shipping charges refundable?</h3>
    <p>Shipping charges are generally non-refundable unless the return is due to our error, such as wrong or defective product shipment.</p>
    <h3>12. What happens if there is a copyright dispute?</h3>
    <p>Books remain the intellectual property of their respective publishers and authors. Content disputes are reviewed according to applicable laws and our Copyright Policy.</p>
    <h3>13. Do you have a privacy policy?</h3>
    <p>Yes. Please refer to our Privacy Policy for details on how customer data is collected, used, and safeguarded.</p>
